Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.76,0:00:02.61,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,It's slippery up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.61,0:00:06.64,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. This church offers \Nthe best view in the area...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.25,0:00:09.28,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,If it doesn't show...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.47,0:00:11.87,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,I'm gonna be pissed at that girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.74,0:00:15.52,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,The demon!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.11,0:00:23.80,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,That's him! There! The demon!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.80,0:00:25.81,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,It's bigger than I expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.81,0:00:27.42,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,You guys evacuate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.68,0:00:30.42,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,If you get caught in the blast,\N you're dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.88,0:00:33.47,Default,Ryoki,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:36.67,Default,Ryoki,0,0,0,,The landing point was way off!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.92,0:00:43.02,italics,Ryoki,0,0,0,,It's big, but also fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.16,0:01:04.94,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,Nice work, Ryoki!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.25,0:01:17.47,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,They did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.47,0:01:19.27,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,It's really where they said it would be!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.27,0:01:21.45,Default,Elisabeth,0,0,0,,Those two are amazing!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.45,0:01:24.15,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,We were right to have them join us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.15,0:01:25.39,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Prince, now!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.43,0:01:27.85,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Well done, Romey.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.23,0:01:30.50,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Everything happened \Nexactly like you planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.36,0:01:33.27,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Hey, is he gonna be okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.27,0:01:34.94,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,The prince is facing it alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.75,0:01:42.07,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,It crushed him!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.17,0:01:52.07,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,You didn't even notice \Nthat you're already dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.07,0:01:54.34,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,You're pretty dense, demon.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.23,0:01:59.54,Default,Ryoki,0,0,0,,Looks like it worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.79,0:02:01.70,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Ryoki, Ekaterina...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.70,0:02:03.01,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Good work.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.78,0:02:04.89,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Are you hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.89,0:02:07.16,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Elisabeth can treat you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.98,0:02:10.98,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,You're talking like \Nthis was your victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.98,0:02:14.27,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Of course not. It's thanks to all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.27,0:02:17.87,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Everyone, let's break down \Nthe monster's body and throw it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.87,0:02:20.95,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Prepare wires and anchors to haul it in.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.95,0:02:23.73,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Everyone, get into position\Nand get ready to start.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.73,0:02:25.56,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,She's no fun to tease.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.04,0:02:35.74,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Heave-ho!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.74,0:02:37.57,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Heave-ho!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.57,0:02:39.00,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Heave-ho!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.80,0:02:43.06,Default,Elisabeth,0,0,0,,I'm glad the three of you\N weren't hurt badly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.06,0:02:46.59,Default,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,Hey, I did pretty good this time, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.59,0:02:48.91,Default,Ryoki,0,0,0,,I did most of the work!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.91,0:02:50.57,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,You all did great!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.72,0:02:57.22,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Lady Romelia?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.60,0:02:59.07,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Lady Romelia?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.51,0:03:01.99,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You don't need bandages anymore, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.99,0:03:04.12,Default,Al,0,0,0,,I'm just fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.12,0:03:07.24,Default,Al,0,0,0,,I'm more scared about losing \Nmy strength after all this rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.47,0:03:10.96,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,That arrogance can \Ncome back to haunt you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.31,0:03:15.67,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Once you're ready to go, \Nwe'll head to Fort Carolus.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.67,0:03:16.96,Default,Both,0,0,0,,Roger that!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.04,0:05:00.39,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,Sir Serbeck! Sir Serbeck!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.39,0:05:03.04,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,I'll take it all!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.04,0:05:04.21,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,Sir Serbeck!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.65,0:05:06.48,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Wh-What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.48,0:05:09.64,Default,Messenger,0,0,0,,The entire demon hunting unit \Nhas just returned safely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.25,0:05:12.71,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Th-That wasn't what was in the reports!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.71,0:05:15.63,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,A-At least {\i1}one{\i0} of them \Nmust be dead, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.62,0:05:18.67,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,They're all unharmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.67,0:05:20.55,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Damn it...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.55,0:05:22.88,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,If even one of them were dead,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.88,0:05:26.39,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,I could make her take the blame \Nand get her out of here,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.39,0:05:30.98,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,maybe even get Count Graham in my debt!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.98,0:05:32.95,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,This way, Administrator.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.72,0:05:38.89,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Face left!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.90,0:05:40.90,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,At ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.44,0:05:51.32,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Thank you for coming to welcome us,\N Administrator Serbeck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.32,0:05:52.75,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's been a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.75,0:05:54.09,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Have you lost weight?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.09,0:05:55.61,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Oh, no...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.27,0:06:00.43,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Um, who are these people?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.43,0:06:01.67,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.76,0:06:06.14,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.14,0:06:10.14,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You were so kind in sending me \Nall the things I've asked for
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.14,0:06:12.48,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,that I brought you a present.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.06,0:06:17.55,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Please read it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.52,0:06:22.53,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's a report about \Nthe taxes here in Cashu,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.53,0:06:24.98,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,and how you've been \Nillegally stealing them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.98,0:06:28.88,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,W-Well... I needed funds to run things...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.88,0:06:31.14,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Everybody does it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.14,0:06:33.97,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Oh my! You do it for \Nthe sake of the people!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.97,0:06:34.95,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,How wonderful!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.45,0:06:39.80,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,These weapons you sold illegally...\NWas that for the people's sake as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.80,0:06:41.45,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,No, this is...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.88,0:06:45.20,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You know, these weapons found \Ntheir way into the hands of bandits,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.20,0:06:47.71,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,and it appears they were used \Nagainst your own people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.10,0:06:49.88,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,But don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.94,0:06:54.13,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Our units have recovered every last one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.13,0:06:57.13,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,As well as the contracts \Nyou made with the bandits.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.13,0:06:59.32,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,They even have your signature here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.80,0:07:03.68,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Illegally selling weapons is treason.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.94,0:07:05.89,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You'll be executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.73,0:07:10.06,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Administrator Serbeck, \Nthis is your last chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.06,0:07:12.94,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,If you turn yourself in, \Nyou'll still be executed,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.94,0:07:16.20,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,but I promise to ask them to delay it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.20,0:07:18.42,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,How dare someone like you...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.80,0:07:21.61,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I know that I'm powerless.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.01,0:07:24.23,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Then shut your mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.23,0:07:28.29,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,I'm not the kind of person who's going to \Nspend his whole life here in the boonies!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.89,0:07:34.03,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,You will be a stepping stone \Non my path to glory, Romelia!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.50,0:07:39.89,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,She's a fake who's just pretending\N to be Lady Romelia!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.89,0:07:42.14,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Beat her down and arrest her!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.14,0:07:43.97,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.97,0:07:45.39,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.12,0:07:49.20,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Um, we're surrounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.20,0:07:51.66,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Is this really okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.66,0:07:53.32,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.75,0:07:54.62,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.76,0:08:07.51,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Ensure there are no casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.51,0:08:08.38,Default,Al/Ray,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.38,0:08:10.15,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,D-Damn it...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.15,0:08:11.25,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.25,0:08:13.77,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Take the girl down and ignore the others!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.61,0:08:21.46,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,M-Magic!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.89,0:08:23.37,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.37,0:08:25.65,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Keep attacking!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.95,0:08:29.35,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Hey, what are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.35,0:08:31.51,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Don't you know who I am?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.51,0:08:34.63,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Damn it! Hey, anyone! Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.17,0:08:36.99,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Serbeck Romes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.99,0:08:39.74,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,By the authority invested \Nin me by the royal capital,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.98,0:08:44.70,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,you are under arrest \Nfor treason and corruption.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.70,0:08:46.94,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,The royal capital...?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.94,0:08:48.41,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.41,0:08:51.74,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You rose all the way \Nto the rank of administrator,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.74,0:08:54.45,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,and this is how you meet your end...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.93,0:08:57.05,Default,Man,0,0,0,,Stand up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.48,0:09:02.24,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,So this was all part of your plot?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.24,0:09:05.07,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,I've done horrible things\N to hold onto my position,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.07,0:09:07.87,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,and now I'm done in by a little girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.87,0:09:09.20,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,All of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.20,0:09:11.53,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,This woman is a witch!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.53,0:09:14.55,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,She deceived the prince and came back \Nfrom the demon continent of Goldea!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.55,0:09:19.04,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,The royal family called off her betrothal \Nand banished her from the capital!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.04,0:09:23.44,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,I thought I'd tasted all the suffering\N this world had to offer,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.44,0:09:26.75,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,but you've been through \Nan even worse hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.75,0:09:27.62,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Take him away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.62,0:09:29.31,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Don't be deceived!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.31,0:09:31.33,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,She's a monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.59,0:09:34.34,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,No matter how loyal you are to her,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.34,0:09:36.97,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,it means nothing to her!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.97,0:09:38.72,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,She'll build you up,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.72,0:09:40.76,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,and when she no longer needs you, \Nshe'll throw you away!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.76,0:09:43.43,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,Someday you'll learn!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.43,0:09:46.34,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,She pretends to be innocent,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.34,0:09:50.65,Default,Serbeck,0,0,0,,but her heart's black!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.58,0:09:54.17,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.56,0:09:57.99,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Nobody believes him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.99,0:09:58.95,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.27,0:10:01.28,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Why do you look so glum?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.63,0:10:02.91,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.91,0:10:04.77,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Into your fortress.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.77,0:10:05.87,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.54,0:10:07.71,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.78,0:10:17.89,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Did you hear that Administrator \NSerbeck was arrested?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.89,0:10:20.63,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,There were so many \Nawful rumors about him...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.98,0:10:22.60,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Who'll take over?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.60,0:10:25.04,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Hmm... I don't remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.04,0:10:28.89,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Supposedly, it's someone who's served \Nthe Grahams for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.13,0:10:32.12,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Nothing will change for us,\N no matter who it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.12,0:10:34.04,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.04,0:10:36.11,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Can I have two of these?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.11,0:10:39.09,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Well, as long as our taxes don't go up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.41,0:10:37.57,top,Cairo,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.12,0:10:44.24,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Please, can you let us through?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.24,0:10:47.03,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,I can't just let you through the gate...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.03,0:10:49.29,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Can you at least give her this gift?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.29,0:10:50.92,Default,Villagers,0,0,0,,Or take a message?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.93,0:10:53.88,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.05,0:10:56.33,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,O-Oh, Lady Cairo?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.33,0:10:58.04,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,Lady Cairo?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.04,0:11:00.65,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,My! What beautiful raspberries!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.65,0:11:03.96,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Did you grow these?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.96,0:11:05.34,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,Oh, uh, yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.34,0:11:09.93,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,The mayor told us to take them to Lady\N Romelia as thanks for saving our village.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.93,0:11:12.10,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Oh, how kind!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.10,0:11:14.25,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.25,0:11:16.51,Default,Villager,0,0,0,,We'd be so happy if you accepted them...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.51,0:11:18.31,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.31,0:11:23.32,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,I'll make sure that she gets them!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.20,0:11:28.72,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Come in...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.00,0:11:32.25,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.50,0:11:35.96,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Why don't you take a little break, ma'am?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.96,0:11:37.26,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.18,0:11:42.22,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,This looks delicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.22,0:11:43.55,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.55,0:11:49.28,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Some villagers brought these raspberries\N as thanks for defeating those monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.28,0:11:52.25,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,so I made a cake from them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.25,0:11:53.52,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Huh...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.23,0:11:56.75,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I hope it wasn't a burden for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.75,0:12:00.78,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,I'll tell them you said thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.78,0:12:01.95,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.54,0:12:05.60,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,How were things \Nin the market, by the way?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.60,0:12:10.25,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Some people were worried \Nabout having a new administrator.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.25,0:12:13.38,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,But that's how it always is \Nwhen something changes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.73,0:12:17.85,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Should I set up a meeting \Nto explain things, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.85,0:12:23.93,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,If I may, I think you're at the limit\N of what you can do alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.93,0:12:28.09,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I-I had Catan take over \Nas administrator for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.10,0:12:33.48,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,He said he wanted to spend \Nhis old age with his wife, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.16,0:12:37.03,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I've caused him so much trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.06,0:12:43.54,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,You've always been bad \Nat relying on others...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.44,0:12:47.51,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Do you remember how when you were a child,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.51,0:12:51.22,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,you had a fight with the daughter \Nof a baron at a garden party?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.22,0:12:52.29,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,A fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.29,0:12:56.40,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Yes. She called you a villainess.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.40,0:12:58.88,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,You could've just told us,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.88,0:13:02.42,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,but instead you ended up knocking \Nher over and climbing on top...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.42,0:13:06.29,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I-I... know I made a mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.29,0:13:07.70,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,And there's more—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.70,0:13:08.74,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,That's enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.74,0:13:10.01,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I have to work!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.91,0:13:13.46,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Did that take your mind off things?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.46,0:13:15.96,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,Don't work too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.96,0:13:18.84,Default,Cairo,0,0,0,,I'll come to get the plate \Nand utensils later.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.23,0:13:23.66,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,She got me good...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.66,0:13:24.94,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,This is delicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.18,0:14:06.61,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,That's the outline of my plan \Nto restore Fort Carolus.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.61,0:14:09.03,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,The fort is in bad \Nfinancial shape already.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.03,0:14:11.01,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,I don't know if we can add more people...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.01,0:14:14.48,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,The demon king's army \Ncontinues to advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.48,0:14:16.93,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,If they breach the northern border,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.93,0:14:19.66,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,they'll take over Cashu instantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.66,0:14:21.53,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,I'm aware.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.53,0:14:23.77,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,But we don't have the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.77,0:14:26.14,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,Right, Financial Magistrate Mary?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.14,0:14:28.55,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,Tax Magistrate Hyde is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.55,0:14:32.18,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,Serbeck's arrest has resulted \Nin a further decrease of our budget.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.18,0:14:36.55,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,We have always been a poor fortress.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.84,0:14:39.85,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,It's hard enough to maintain \Na fort of this size...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.85,0:14:41.31,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.31,0:14:43.95,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,So I have a plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.99,0:14:47.46,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,This is... Guillier Gorge?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.54,0:14:51.20,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You're aware of it, yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.66,0:14:53.81,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Troop Magistrate Dars.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.12,0:14:56.70,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,Guillier is a very dangerous place.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.07,0:15:03.19,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,There are many raptors there,\Nso we bar the people from entering.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.19,0:15:05.97,Default,Graves,0,0,0,,I'm told that we once sent \Na unit to fight them
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.97,0:15:07.97,Default,Graves,0,0,0,,and many died there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.19,0:15:10.23,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,When I was journeying \Nto defeat the demon king,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.23,0:15:12.88,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I crossed the Gaela Mountains there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.88,0:15:14.37,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,If we send enough forces—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.40,0:15:16.53,top,Dars,0,0,0,,You were only able to do that \Nwith the prince's help!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.14,0:15:20.78,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's said that there's \Na vein of gold here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.03,0:15:23.73,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,If we're to deal with \Nour financial issues,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.73,0:15:25.21,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,we need something new.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.21,0:15:26.32,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,Are you mad?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.32,0:15:30.69,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,We don't have troops to spare \Non some story the miners tell!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.69,0:15:35.72,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,You were the one who just said that Cashu \Nwas already in danger, Lady Romelia.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.72,0:15:39.16,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,I cannot agree to something \Nthat will waste our soldiers' lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.16,0:15:43.36,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,If we put even more strain on our budget\N and have to increase taxes,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.36,0:15:46.05,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,we might upset the people, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.05,0:15:47.46,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.66,0:15:50.04,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I'll attempt to find \Nanother way to rebuild.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.24,0:15:55.05,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,That's all for today, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.34,0:16:02.63,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,You can look all you like, but you \Nwon't find money for the expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.63,0:16:04.89,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,We have to cut everywhere \Nwe possibly can.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.89,0:16:07.57,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,That's what it means to be in wartime.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.84,0:16:12.20,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Fort Carolus's finances do seem to be \Nin a better state now, thanks to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.20,0:16:15.32,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,We can't let the soldiers starve.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.32,0:16:16.57,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.86,0:16:19.33,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,What will you do now, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.57,0:16:23.55,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Can I take a look at all our books?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.69,0:16:28.88,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,Financial Magistrate Mary is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.88,0:16:32.38,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,If we submit our real books, \Nwe'll be deemed bankrupt.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.89,0:16:36.21,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,But if we lie, we'll be shut down.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.46,0:16:41.06,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,So if I leave the numbers as they are, \Nand just make the text harder to read...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.40,0:16:44.05,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,The worst we'd get is a fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.64,0:16:46.66,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,But it's not enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.11,0:16:49.74,italics,Romelia,0,0,0,,We'll need to talk to the merchants.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.76,0:16:51.70,Default,Al,0,0,0,,You there!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.70,0:16:53.02,Default,Al,0,0,0,,No gaps in the shield wall!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.02,0:16:54.08,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Hold your shield properly!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.08,0:16:55.55,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Match the angle of your spears!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.55,0:16:56.24,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Left flank!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.24,0:16:58.17,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Your feet aren't lined up!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.02,0:17:06.76,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,How did it go?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.76,0:17:09.51,Default,Al,0,0,0,,We won decisively!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.80,0:17:11.17,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.17,0:17:14.09,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Um, about our training plan for today...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.34,0:17:17.91,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Some of the troops have yet to see \Nreal combat and can't keep up with us...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.91,0:17:22.46,Default,Al,0,0,0,,The other unit commanders asked us\N to come up with a new plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.75,0:17:23.90,Default,Al,0,0,0,,What will we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.31,0:17:26.83,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,Don't worry!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.83,0:17:28.91,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,I have defeated the demon!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.75,0:17:32.31,flashback,Villagers,0,0,0,,I know he wants a ship, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.31,0:17:35.65,flashback,Villagers,0,0,0,,That demon destroyed \Nall the ships we have.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.65,0:17:39.83,flashback,Villagers,0,0,0,,And the sea's gonna be \Nstormy for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.83,0:17:42.11,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,Is it dangerous to leave port now?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.47,0:17:46.76,flashback,Ekaterina,0,0,0,,Romelia, that merchant ship\N is leaving today.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.61,0:17:50.02,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,I see!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.02,0:17:52.47,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,A storm wouldn't bother \Nthis thing at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.73,0:17:55.20,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,Nice job finding it, Ekaterina!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.26,0:17:59.63,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,Look at all that cargo...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.63,0:18:02.19,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,Is it okay to carry that much?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.19,0:18:04.72,flashback,Ryoki,0,0,0,,The port's been shut down for so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.72,0:18:07.50,flashback,Ryoki,0,0,0,,They need to do all they can \Nto recoup their losses.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.50,0:18:11.17,flashback,Elisabeth,0,0,0,,But this is one of the \Nworld's biggest ports.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.17,0:18:13.48,flashback,Elisabeth,0,0,0,,They know what they're doing.\N They'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.48,0:18:15.27,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,But the fishermen—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.27,0:18:16.22,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,Romelia.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.62,0:18:21.32,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,Every minute we waste, \Nthe demons are advancing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.60,0:18:23.79,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,You need to be willing \Nto take risks, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.98,0:18:27.39,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Commander Romey?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.15,0:18:29.77,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.13,0:18:33.07,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,No, it's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.07,0:18:35.57,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I'll let you two decide \Nwhat to do with the training.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.57,0:18:36.90,Default,Both,0,0,0,,Understood!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.04,0:18:43.48,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Hello there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.48,0:18:45.05,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,L-Lady Romelia!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.31,0:18:46.86,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,Good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.86,0:18:49.59,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,There's something I wanted to check.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.59,0:18:50.76,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.76,0:18:56.18,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Can you gather up all the records of\N the expedition to Guillier Gorge for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.18,0:18:58.06,Default,Dars,0,0,0,,All of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.06,0:18:59.16,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.16,0:19:02.47,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Can you do it, Troop Magistrate Dars?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.77,0:19:04.73,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,I'm so tired!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.73,0:19:07.88,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,We got promoted, but we still \Ndon't get our own rooms?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.88,0:19:10.62,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Lady Romelia seemed tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.62,0:19:11.75,Default,Ray,0,0,0,,Is she okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.97,0:19:15.09,Default,Al,0,0,0,,She's probably dealing with \Nthe mess Serbeck left behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.52,0:19:20.26,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Either way, we just need \Nto do our own jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.20,0:19:25.63,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,So, did you find a way \Nto come up with the money?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.63,0:19:26.64,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Thanks to all your help,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.91,0:19:30.93,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I've realized that it will be difficult to\Nfind the money from within the fortress.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.44,0:19:36.35,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,At the same time, I've found \Nsomething concerning...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.24,0:19:38.64,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,That list?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.15,0:19:44.33,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,This is the list of soldiers who went \Nto Guillier, as proposed by Hyde.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.82,0:19:49.43,Default,Graves,0,0,0,,It's supposed to be Troop Magistrate Dars\N who decides who goes..
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.43,0:19:50.59,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.59,0:19:53.09,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,But his list was rejected.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.09,0:19:58.85,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You were told to send fresh recruits \Nfrom poor houses, it seems.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.85,0:20:00.17,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.17,0:20:03.76,Default,Graves,0,0,0,,Was it an attempt to reduce \Nthe amount of mouths to feed?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.76,0:20:07.74,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You made this list, yes, \NTax Magistrate Hyde?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.74,0:20:11.11,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,I-I just did what Administrator \NSerbeck told me...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.11,0:20:14.40,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You must've known exactly \Nwhat it would be used for.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.20,0:20:19.77,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,When the war began, \Neverything changed here in Cashu.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.12,0:20:24.03,Default,Hyde,0,0,0,,I... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.03,0:20:28.00,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,Just maintaining the troops we had \Nwas eating away at our funds.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.00,0:20:32.46,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,If we didn't want to raise taxes, \Nwe were told to find another way.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.84,0:20:36.78,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,He's not the only one who should \Nbe held responsible for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.99,0:20:41.07,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I'm not interested in \Ndiscussing past failures.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.39,0:20:45.63,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,What I want to discuss now \Nis how we rebuild Fort Carolus.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.04,0:20:47.20,Default,Graves,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.57,0:20:50.60,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Serbeck's records of the \Ninvestigations into Guillier.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.00,0:20:52.96,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,The geography. The raptors' \Nlocations and habits.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.96,0:20:55.64,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,The best locations to build a fort.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.64,0:20:59.78,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,There's a surprising amount of detail \Nabout the plans they had then.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.20,0:21:03.11,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,The plan failed,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.11,0:21:07.06,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,but with this, we can fight while \Nprotecting ourselves from the raptors.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.06,0:21:09.37,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,But during the last expedition,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.37,0:21:13.19,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,the raptors devoured the men \Nbefore they could build a fort.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.28,0:21:21.72,flashback,Elisabeth,0,0,0,,Prince Henri!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.74,0:21:31.43,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I'll send my own soldiers to Guillier\N so that doesn't happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.97,0:21:33.47,Default,Graves,0,0,0,,The Romey unit?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.47,0:21:37.58,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Everything in Carolus will get better\N if we find that gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.58,0:21:41.48,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,You're sacrificing your personal soldiers
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.48,0:21:44.70,Default,Mary,0,0,0,,to find gold that might \Nnot even be there?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.70,0:21:46.56,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.56,0:21:49.04,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,That's why I trained them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.22,0:21:55.46,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,It's time for our next mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.46,0:21:57.44,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,The location is Guillier Gorge.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.44,0:21:59.67,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,We'll defeat the demons that dwell there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.99,0:22:02.37,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,Guillier is a rock-filled wasteland.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.37,0:22:06.07,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,And in the past, many soldiers \Nhave been defeated there.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.02,0:22:10.97,flashback,Henri,0,0,0,,Romelia! Give me your hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.97,0:22:12.26,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.76,0:22:18.89,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,A brutal battle awaits you there.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.32,0:22:25.73,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,But the soldiers of Carolus who died \Nthere have left us much knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.03,0:22:28.75,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,I'll entrust all of it to you!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.18,0:22:32.26,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You've been victorious so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.26,0:22:35.54,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,You'll be able to succeed in \Ndefeating the demons at Guillier.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.89,0:22:39.78,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,But do you know what will happen \Nif you take victory for granted?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.46,0:22:44.78,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,The proud... meet destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.01,0:22:47.68,Default,Al,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.29,0:22:53.43,Default,Al,0,0,0,,We promise to bring back a victory \Nworthy of the things you've done for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.60,0:22:59.54,Default,Romelia,0,0,0,,All right, I'll be going.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.24,0:23:10.36,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.36,0:23:11.84,flashback,Romelia,0,0,0,,Prince Henri!

